  "content": {
    "id": "p33-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Find $a$ for which the cubic equation $x^3-ax^2+bx-4=0$ has three positive integer roots.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=5$ or $a=6$.\n\nThe positive integer root triples have product $4$; their sums give $a$.",
      "worked": "Let the roots be $p$, $q$ and $r$. By Vieta’s formulas,\n$$\\begin{align*}pqr&=4,\\\\p+q+r&=a.\\end{align*}$$\nThe only positive integer triples with product $4$, apart from order, are $(1,1,4)$ and $(1,2,2)$. Repeated roots are allowed.\n$$\\begin{align*}a&=1+1+4=6\\quad\\text{or}\\\\a&=1+2+2=5.\\end{align*}$$\nHence $a=5$ or $a=6$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 43
  },
